<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<StyleSet xmlns="http://adamantium/ui"
          xmlns:x="http://adamantium/ui/xaml/extensions">

    <!-- THE FOCUS RING for the whole application: what the keyboard leaves around the control it reached. One style is
         the focus visual of every control; a control wanting its own sets FocusVisualStyle, which is applied after this
         and wins.

         Two things differ from Fluent, and both are decisions rather than sizes.

         SQUARE ALWAYS. Fluent's ring traces the adorned control's own rounding (AdornedCornerRadius) so it stays
         parallel to the edge it follows. Here the ring does NOT follow the control: every control in this theme is
         square already, and a ring that adapts its geometry to whatever it lands on is a ring whose shape carries no
         information. It is the same mark everywhere, which is what makes it read as one thing.

         THE DARK LINE GOES OUTSIDE. Fluent puts a thin dark line INSIDE the accent one, to keep the ring legible on an
         accent-filled button. That works, but it eats a pixel of the control it surrounds - at this theme's weights the
         control is small enough for that pixel to matter. Outside, the dark line does the same separating job against
         the accent fill and instead spends its pixel on the panel, where there is nothing to lose. -->

    <Style Selector="FocusAdorner">
        <!-- Room for the outer separator, which is the only part standing off the control's own outline. -->
        <Setter Property="Outset" Value="{ResourceReference FocusRingOutset}"/>
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <Setter.Value>
                <ControlTemplate TargetType="FocusAdorner">
                    <!-- Siblings in a Grid rather than nested borders: each line is placed by its own margin instead of
                         by whatever inset the other gives a child. -->
                    <Grid IsHitTestVisible="False">
                        <Border BorderThickness="{ResourceReference StrokeThin}"
                                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource FocusStrokeColorInner}"
                                CornerRadius="0"/>
                        <Border Margin="{ResourceReference StrokeThin}"
                                BorderThickness="{ResourceReference StrokeThin}"
                                BorderBrush="{ThemeResource AccentFillColorDefault}"
                                CornerRadius="0"/>
                    </Grid>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter.Value>
        </Setter>
    </Style>

</StyleSet>
